      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(heartbeat): bound HEARTBEAT.md file read size",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`resolveHeartbeatPreflight` in `src/infra/heartbeat-runner.ts` read the workspace `HEARTBEAT.md` with an unbounded `fs.readFile`, allowing an arbitrarily large file to be loaded into memory and processed by the heartbeat pipeline.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nSwitch to `readRegularFile` with a 16 MiB cap so the read is bounded and rejects symlinks and non-files. This aligns with other bounded-read fixes in the repo and prevents accidental or malicious oversized heartbeat files from causing memory pressure.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOversized `HEARTBEAT.md` files are now treated like missing files: the heartbeat run continues without the file content. Normal-sized heartbeat files behave exactly as before.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Added `src/infra/heartbeat-runner.oversized-heartbeat-file.test.ts` with a regression test using a `16 MiB + 1` byte file and asserting the run continues.\n- Local focused run: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/infra/heartbeat-runner.oversized-heartbeat-file.test.ts --run` passes (1/1 tests).\n- `oxlint` clean on changed files.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n```text\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/infra/heartbeat-runner.oversized-heartbeat-file.test.ts --run\n[test] starting test/vitest/vitest.infra.config.ts\n RUN  v4.1.9\n ✓ |infra| src/infra/heartbeat-runner.oversized-heartbeat-file.test.ts (1 test) 286ms\n     ✓ treats an oversized HEARTBEAT.md like a missing file and continues the run\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  1 passed (1)\n[test] passed 1 Vitest shard in 9.12s\n```\n",
        "branch": "fix/bound-heartbeat-file-read",
        "head_sha": "f3c90074be8fe1f614f5b24845b310f76b608566",
        "author": "cxbasdev",
